{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"HB0036","billNumberShort":"H.B. 36","billNumberLong":"HB0036S01","fileNumber":"2026FL1021","shortTitle":"Gold Medal Schools Pilot Program","currentSubVersion":"1","currentMinVersion":"3","primeSponsor":"HALLK","primeSponsorName":"Rep. Hall, Katy","primeSponsorHouse":"H","floorSponsor":"STRATKJ","floorSponsorName":"Sen. Stratton, Keven J.","floorSponsorHouse":"S","generalProvisions":"This bill creates the Gold Medal Schools Pilot Program.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>defines terms;<hr><ltbullet>creates a five-year pilot program known as the Gold Medal Schools Pilot Program to:<hr><ltbullet1>promote physical activity in an eligible school; and<hr><ltbullet1>promote healthy eating habits in an eligible school;<hr><ltbullet>requires the State Board of Education to:<hr><ltbullet1>administer the program;<hr><ltbullet1>select an eligible school for participation in the program; and<hr><ltbullet1>award program funds;<hr><ltbullet>creates a reporting requirement;<hr><ltbullet>creates a cap for administrative costs associated with the program;<hr><ltbullet>creates a sunset date for the program; and<hr><ltbullet>makes technical and conforming changes.","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"Tyler Keetch","fiscalAnalyst":"Kiki Hudson","lastAction":"Governor Signed","lastActionOwner":"Lieutenant Governor's office for filing","lastActionDate":"3/19/2026","trackingID":"UORRYKAVEQ","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"Bill Numbered but not Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2025-12-15 16:54:36.597","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LNUMBER","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"Numbered Bill Publicly Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2025-12-15 16:54:36.613","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LL